{
  "chapter": "reliability/error-taxonomy",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "Classification happens at the adapter, from a stable code the catalogue owns, never by",
    "matching vendor prose that changes without notice.",
    "Five classes and one question each: who can fix it. Waiting fixes transient, you fix",
    "permanent, a person fixes policy, a decision fixes budget, and nothing here fixes",
    "semantic because nothing raised.",
    "Every error has two audiences. The model sees an error only when it can act on it: its",
    "own mistake, a refusal it must stop working around, or a budget it must conclude",
    "within. A recovered transient never reaches it, or it starts reasoning about network",
    "conditions and retries the call itself.",
    "Retry-After is captured where it exists and nowhere later, and it means nothing on a",
    "class that will not be retried.",
    "Budget and semantic are absent from the error rate: one is the system working, the",
    "other never raised. Which makes the error rate a floor."
  ],
  "catalogue": {
    "rate_limited": { "class": "transient", "blame": "world" },
    "provider_unavailable": { "class": "transient", "blame": "world" },
    "context_too_long": { "class": "permanent", "blame": "you" },
    "adapter_type_error": { "class": "permanent", "blame": "you" },
    "account_not_found": { "class": "permanent", "blame": "model" },
    "unknown_tool": { "class": "permanent", "blame": "model" },
    "refused": { "class": "policy", "blame": "person" },
    "approval_required": { "class": "policy", "blame": "person" },
    "cost_cap_reached": { "class": "budget", "blame": "limit" },
    "max_turns": { "class": "budget", "blame": "limit" },
    "wrong_policy_quoted": { "class": "semantic", "blame": "nobody" }
  },
